-- and the completion pass of 2026-11-04 moved out of `inert`.
--
-- Where the expected values come from.
--
-- * Every expected value is written by hand from the Code's words (the raw line numbers are in pc-general-moved.l4 above each function).
--   None is copied from output.
-- * Each function is tested on both sides of each of its limbs.  A "yes" the text states in its own words is JUST TRUE; a "no" the text
--   states in its own words is JUST FALSE; every other case is NOTHING and is asserted to be NOTHING, because a caller who turns
--   NOTHING into FALSE has read the text as saying what it does not say (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- * The Code's Illustrations to ss 6, 33, 36 and 38 are tested against the functions of the Code they speak of.
-- * A failing assertion is a finding.  None has been edited to match the code.
